      en: "Tubli Bay is a shallow marine bay in eastern Bahrain, known as an important wetland. It is a key stopover for migratory birds and hosts diverse marine life. The bay features mangrove forests and mudflats. Recent efforts have aimed to protect the bay from pollution. Tubli Bay is popular among birdwatchers and nature enthusiasts. It also contains remnants of historic pearl fishing villages. The bay is part of the national protected area network. It serves as an important spawning ground for fish and crustaceans.",
