      en: "Jaradah Island is a transient sandbar in the Gulf of Bahrain, 15 km northeast of Manama. It emerges only at low tide, stretching 4 km in length and 1 km in width. The island is composed of biogenic sand from coral and shell fragments. Tidal pools form during low water, hosting brittle stars, hermit crabs, and numerous gastropods. It serves as a roosting site for terns and gulls. Jaradah is a unique destination for tidal flat walking and marine wildlife photography, accessible only by boat during specific tidal windows.",
